# Line 1 of this file read, from 2026-08-31 until now:
#   anchor-interface-account insecure UNAVAILABLE rc=0 no-parseable-output
# It was wrong, and it was wrong in the direction that would have taken a real zero
# out of Radar's denominator. The runner that wrote this file decided ok versus
# UNAVAILABLE by asking whether radar had written an output file. radar writes no
# output file when it finds nothing, so a clean zero and a failed run look identical
# to that test. radar's own stdout for this run, kept at
# raw/radar-c2-2026-08-31-stdout/anchor-interface-account.insecure.log, says:
